    "title": "Brookshire's donates $40K to CHRISTUS Children's Miracle Network - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Avery Peck ,\n2 hours ago\nTYLER, Texas ( KETK ) — CHRISTUS Health honored its longstanding partnership with Brookshire’s Grocery Company on Wednesday, celebrating a relationship that has supported children’s health care in East Texas for nearly four decades.\nCHRISTUS Health hosts ribbon-cutting ceremony for new Sulphur Springs facility During the event, Brookshire’s presented CHRISTUS Health with a $40,000 donation benefiting the Children’s Miracle Network. The contribution adds to a legacy of giving that now exceeds $3 million over 38 years.\nThe partnership began in 1988, just one year after Mother Francis Hospital became the Tyler area’s first designated Miracle Network Hospital. This milestone also launched what is now Brookshire’s longest-running charitable partnership.\n“We know the importance of what the care teams do here every single day,” Morgan Jones, Senior Manager of Communications with Brookshire’s, said. “To be able to support them in their daily operations and growing is incredible.”\nJones added that sharing in the impact of these donations is “a wonderful opportunity.”",
